CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ empty && fold yields true: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ empty \|\| fold yields false: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ empty binary fold yields the init operand: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
[expr.prim.fold]/3: folds over an empty pack yield the operator's identity
(unary && / ||) or the init operand (binary); previously the empty-pack
instantiation left residual fold nodes that degraded the function body to
nondeterministic values.  Runtime-verified against g++ and clang++.
